perl 5.44.0 (with perl-cross 1.6.5 laid over it) for the collaboCore guest, which has no fork():

- doio.c, util.c, perl.h: system(), qx// and piped opens (list and string forms) start their
  children with posix_spawn. pp_system's non-fork path calls do_aspawn and do_spawn, as it does on
  Windows and VMS; my_popen and my_popen_list spawn instead of forking. Which program runs is
  decided as do_exec3 and do_aexec5 decide what to exec (the shell only for shell metacharacters,
  a trailing 2>&1 kept as a dup2, ENOEXEC falling back to the shell); a failed spawn warns "Can't
  exec" and returns -1 with errno, as the fork path reports a failed exec. fork itself stays
  unsupported ("The fork function is unimplemented"), and so does open(FH, "-|"). system(1, LIST)
  spawns without waiting and returns the pid, as on Windows.
- ext/re/re_top.h: regcomp's helpers that are not static since 5.43 renamed in the re extension's
  copy, as the others there are; a static link (all extensions in perl) otherwise has them twice.
- Makefile (perl-cross's): a static extension's make also runs pm_to_blib; MakeMaker's static
  target no longer does, so its .pm files (POSIX.pm, List/Util.pm, ...) were never put in lib/.
- ext/IPC-Open3: open3 and open2 spawn as on Windows where perl has no fork (system(1, LIST));
  pp_sys.c keeps system's numeric arguments numeric for it, as on Windows.
--- a/doio.c
